    "narrative": "Ghost Ride the WHIP enters today\u2019s slate with **Corbin Carroll** standing as our undisputed anchor at an 84.65 efficiency rating. Facing Keller, M, **Corbin Carroll** benefits from a high-upside matchup against a vulnerable arm; despite a minor downgrade for the opposing catcher\u2019s pop time, the combination of his leadoff spot and the projected run environment keeps him in elite territory. **James Wood** (78.42) also projects as a high-octane play, leveraging a massive 5.89 xERA from Scherzer to solidify his status as a must-start. Both players are expected to be our primary engines for SB production, our scarcest category, as they exploit the specific delivery patterns of their respective matchups to push for extra bases.\n\nThe most difficult roster decision landed on **Zach McKinstry**, who remained on the bench with a 49.20 score. While his park factors and SP matchup were favorable, he ultimately fell short of the threshold needed to unseat **Henry Bolte** or **Austin Riley**, as his negative platoon adjustment against Bradish eroded his base efficiency. Elsewhere, we are leaning heavily into **Jose Caballero** (71.83) and **Isaac Paredes** (71.15), both of whom benefit from optimal platoon splits today. While **Austin Riley** (54.87) faces a challenging 1.87s catcher pop time that slightly limits his upside, his baseline profile remains sufficient to start over our limited bench depth.\n\nWe have several situational flags to monitor throughout the afternoon. **Cole Young** is locked in at the leadoff spot against Rocker, and while his score is a respectable 54.57, the matchup requires close attention as Rocker\u2019s secondary stuff could neutralize his speed advantage if he fails to reach base early. Additionally, while **Tyler Soderstrom** carries a strong 58.21 score aided by favorable park factors, the 3.69 xERA of Tolle represents a tier of pitcher that could dampen his output compared to the rest of the outfield corps. We are effectively sitting the remainder of our depth\u2014including the inactive **Vinnie Pasquantino**, **Mickey Moniak**, and the injured **Trevor Story**\u2014to protect our remaining game caps for higher-leverage opportunities later in the week.",
